ogic conclusions, factual attributions, entity-attribute claims). Two tracks: (a) REAL claims the models can plausibly derive/read; (b) SYNTHETIC novel-entity claims with stipulated ground truth to control priors. For each claim create MATCHED conditions with identical verbatim proposition at the read-out point: (i) SELF-AUTHORED — elicit the claim as the model's own conclusion via a short CoT/derivation ('Reason step by step, then state your conclusion'), then read internal belief at the model-produced conclusion token; (ii) EXTERNAL — the identical conclusion sentence is supplied verbatim as given text ('Here is a statement: <claim>') from a neutral source, and belief is read at the same tokens. Control conditions: (iii) EXTERNAL-ATTRIBUTED-TO-SELF (text says 'You previously concluded: <claim>' without the model actually generating it) to separate authorship from mere self-attribution; (iv) LENGTH/EFFORT-MATCHED external (a filler derivation precedes the external claim) to control for context length and preceding reasoning tokens. Include comprehension checks and paraphrase/format perturbations. 2) Internal belief probing: For Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B, Mistral-7B, extract residual-stream and per-head activations at the claim tokens across layers; train linear BELIEF probes (P(claim true)) and a representation-based CONFIDENCE probe, with shuffled-label control tasks; report per-layer accuracy/AUROC. 3) Endowment measurement: Define authorship-endowment = belief(SELF-AUTHORED) − belief(EXTERNAL) per item and layer. Test the key prediction that endowment > 0 for BOTH true and false claims (positive even for FALSE self-generated claims → not rational evidence accumulation). Verify control conditions: mere self-attribution (iii) yields smaller endowment than genuine generation, and length-matched (iv) rules out context-length confounds. 4) Truth-independence & geometry: Quantify the truth-independent endowment (belief shift after conditioning on ground truth