Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "recognition_truth_leak", "Title": "It Feels Familiar, So It Must Be True: A Recognition-to-Truth Leak in LLM Beliefs", "Short Hypothesis": "Mirroring the human recognition-based truth effect (statements that merely feel recognized are judged truer, an effect that outweighs actual repetition), an LLM's internally-decoded belief in a claim's TRUTH is inflated by its internal FAMILIARITY/RECOGNITION signal for the claim's entity, independent of (and even against) whether the model actually knows the relevant fact. This recognition-to-truth leak is linearly decodable, largely orthogonal to whether the fact is genuinely known, predicts familiarity-driven hallucination, and is carried by an identifiable component that can be steered to decouple recognition from truth.", "Related Work": "Human research establishes a recognition-based truth effect: statements JUDGED old (recognized) receive higher truth ratings, and this effect exceeds the effect of actual factual repetition (Recognition-based truth effect 2023); prospective feeling-of-knowing (FOK) is dissociable from actual knowledge and can rest on mere cue-familiarity rather than target-accessibility (FOK & partial knowledge 2016; metacognitive domain specificity 2020). In LLM interpretability, sparse-autoencoder 'entity recognition / knowledge-awareness' directions detect whether the model recognizes an entity and causally gate refusal/hallucination (Do I Know This Entity? 2024); 'factual self-awareness' linear features predict correct recall (Factual Self-Awareness 2025); internal states encode the knowledge-RECALL PROCESS, not truthfulness, so associated hallucinations look like facts (LLMs Do NOT Know What They Don't Know 2025); and truth is linearly decodable (Geometry of Truth 2023). CRITICALLY, none ask whether the RECOGNITION/FAMILIARITY signal CONTAMINATES the TRUTH judgment \u2014 whether merely recognizing an entity inflates the internally-decoded belief that a claim about it is true, independent of actual knowledge. Prior recognition work links recognition to refusal/hallucination-likelihood, not to a truth-inflation bias; my prior illusory-truth proposal concerns IN-CONTEXT repetition, whereas here the source is PARAMETRIC recognition/familiarity. We transfer the canonical recognition-based truth effect into LLM belief internals with a mechanistic, causal treatment.", "Abstract": "People rate statements they merely recognize as truer, even when recognition carries no diagnostic information \u2014 a recognition-based truth effect that can outweigh the effect of genuine repetition, and a cousin of the feeling-of-knowing that rests on cue-familiarity rather than real knowledge. LLMs are known to encode an entity-recognition signal (whether they 'know' a subject) and a separate truth signal, and to hallucinate confidently about familiar-but-unknown entities. We ask a sharper, mechanistic question: does the model's recognition/familiarity signal leak into and inflate its belief in a claim's truth, independent of whether it actually knows the relevant fact? We hypothesize that (i) an entity-recognition/familiarity channel and a truth channel are separately linearly decodable, (ii) the recognition channel contaminates the truth channel \u2014 claims about recognized entities are internally believed truer, holding actual knowledge constant \u2014 an internal signature of the recognition-based truth effect, (iii) the leak is graded with familiarity and largest when the model recognizes the entity but lacks the specific fact, predicting familiarity-driven (associated) hallucination, and (iv) the leak is carried by an identifiable component that can be steered to decouple recognition from truth. We build a controlled dataset crossing entity FAMILIARITY (recognized/popular vs. unrecognized/rare, plus synthetic entities) with claim VERACITY (true/false) and KNOWLEDGE status (fact actually known vs. not). On frozen open-weight models (Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B, Mistral-7B) we train linear probes to decode recognition, truth, and knowledge, measure their geometry, quantify a per-claim recognition-to-truth leak, test its predictiveness for hallucination, localize the responsible heads via activation patching, and test causal steering. Metrics: probe accuracy/AUROC, subspace angle, projected-out decodability, leak magnitude, leak\u2013hallucination AUROC, patching effect sizes, post-steering decoupling, and perplexity.", "Experiments": "1) Dataset construction: Generate ~6k subject-relation-attribute claims crossing three factors. (A) ENTITY FAMILIARITY: highly-recognized/popular entities (frequent in pretraining), low-familiarity/rare real entities, and fully SYNTHETIC novel entities (never seen) to anchor the unrecognized end. (B) CLAIM VERACITY: true vs. false attribute claims. (C) KNOWLEDGE status: whether the model actually knows the correct attribute (measured empirically by closed-book accuracy). Crucially include the diagnostic RECOGNIZED-BUT-UNKNOWN cell (familiar entity, but the specific fact is not reliably recalled) versus RECOGNIZED-AND-KNOWN and UNRECOGNIZED cells. Use subject-popularity/frequency estimates to set familiarity, and match claim surface form across familiarity levels (paraphrase/format perturbations) to guard against lexical confounds. Add a behavioral TRUTH-JUDGMENT probe ('Is this claim true? + confidence') and comprehension checks. Human-validate a sample. 2) Three-channel probing: For Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B, Mistral-7B, extract residual-stream and per-head activations at the entity/attribute tokens across layers, WITHOUT asking the truth question. Following prior entity-recognition and truth-probe methods, train linear probes for (R) RECOGNITION/FAMILIARITY (recognized vs. unrecognized entity), (T) TRUTH-VALUE (true vs. false claim), and (K) KNOWLEDGE (will the model correctly recall this fact), with shuffled-label control tasks; report per-layer accuracy/AUROC. 3) Geometry: Compute cosine/subspace angle between the recognition, truth, and knowledge directions; test whether truth remains decodable after projecting out recognition (and vice versa), and whether recognition is distinct from the genuine-knowledge direction, to characterize the leak's source. 4) Recognition-to-truth leak (key test): Define per-claim leak = shift of the internal truth readout toward 'true' as a function of entity recognition, holding knowledge and veracity constant (comparing recognized-but-unknown vs. unrecognized cells for matched FALSE claims). Test leak > 0 across models versus a recognition-independent null; confirm the strongest leak in the RECOGNIZED-BUT-UNKNOWN cell (familiarity without diagnostic knowledge), mirroring the human cue-familiarity FOK. Replicate the human finding that recognition's effect on internal truth exceeds a matched in-context-repetition manipulation. Compare internal leak to stated truth judgments (behavioral recognition-based truth effect). 5) Predictiveness: Test whether the internal leak (read before any query) predicts familiarity-driven associated hallucination (confidently asserting a false attribute about a recognized entity) via AUROC, beyond a log-prob baseline and beyond the knowledge probe. 6) Localization: Use activation patching / causal mediation to find heads/layers that transport the recognition signal into the truth channel (patch recognized-entity activations into unrecognized-entity runs and vice versa; find the minimal component that raises/lowers the truth readout); compare to entity-recognition SAE directions and truth/belief heads from prior work. 7) Causal control: Derive a contrastive 'recognition-to-truth leak' steering direction (recognized vs. unrecognized activations, controlling for knowledge). Test (a) subtracting it decouples recognition from truth \u2014 lowering unwarranted belief in false claims about recognized entities and reducing associated hallucination; (b) amplifying it exaggerates the leak; (c) specificity: random-direction and truth-direction steering do not selectively decouple, and genuine-knowledge recall is preserved; (d) collateral checks on general benchmarks (MMLU subset), known-fact accuracy, and perplexity. 8) Generalization: Test probe/steering transfer across entity types (people, places, works, organizations), familiarity levels, and real vs. synthetic entities. Metrics: probe accuracy/AUROC, subspace angle and projected-out decodability, recognition-to-truth leak magnitude and sign, recognition-vs-repetition comparison, internal-vs-verbal gap, leak\u2013hallucination AUROC (vs. log-prob and knowledge baselines), patching logit-difference effect sizes, post-steering decoupling and specificity, perplexity/benchmark deltas.", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "The leak could reflect legitimate inference (claims about popular entities are, on average, more likely to be true in training data) rather than a spurious recognition-to-truth contamination; the FALSE-claim cells (where recognition and truth diverge), the matched RECOGNIZED-BUT-UNKNOWN vs. UNRECOGNIZED comparison at held-constant veracity/knowledge, and the synthetic-entity anchor are designed to isolate genuine leakage from valid frequency-based inference (though full separation is difficult). The recognition and knowledge channels may be hard to separate (recognition often co-occurs with knowledge); the recognized-but-unknown cell and projected-out analyses are built to dissociate them, and even a characterization of entanglement is informative and directly engages the 'recall-process-not-truth' finding. The effect may be absent internally \u2014 a robust negative result (recognition does not contaminate the truth channel) would itself be a valuable, publishable finding contrasting with the human recognition-based truth effect. Familiarity estimated from subject popularity is noisy; we use multiple frequency proxies and the synthetic anchor. The truth/recognition probes may not be cleanly linear at every layer; we report layerwise results with control tasks. The leak component may be distributed rather than a discrete head; we treat 'steer to decouple recognition from truth' as the causal test rather than pinning an exact head. Steering could degrade fluency or make the model distrust all familiar content; we use small magnitudes, random/truth-direction baselines, and monitor perplexity, known-fact accuracy, and general benchmarks. Results may not transfer to very large closed models."}}
Proposal finalized: {'Name': 'recognition_truth_leak', 'Title': 'It Feels Familiar, So It Must Be True: A Recognition-to-Truth Leak in LLM Beliefs', 'Short Hypothesis': "Mirroring the human recognition-based truth effect (statements that merely feel recognized are judged truer, an effect that outweighs actual repetition), an LLM's internally-decoded belief in a claim's TRUTH is inflated by its internal FAMILIARITY/RECOGNITION signal for the claim's entity, independent of (and even against) whether the model actually knows the relevant fact. This recognition-to-truth leak is linearly decodable, largely orthogonal to whether the fact is genuinely known, predicts familiarity-driven hallucination, and is carried by an identifiable component that can be steered to decouple recognition from truth.", 'Related Work': "Human research establishes a recognition-based truth effect: statements JUDGED old (recognized) receive higher truth ratings, and this effect exceeds the effect of actual factual repetition (Recognition-based truth effect 2023); prospective feeling-of-knowing (FOK) is dissociable from actual knowledge and can rest on mere cue-familiarity rather than target-accessibility (FOK & partial knowledge 2016; metacognitive domain specificity 2020). In LLM interpretability, sparse-autoencoder 'entity recognition / knowledge-awareness' directions detect whether the model recognizes an entity and causally gate refusal/hallucination (Do I Know This Entity? 2024); 'factual self-awareness' linear features predict correct recall (Factual Self-Awareness 2025); internal states encode the knowledge-RECALL PROCESS, not truthfulness, so associated hallucinations look like facts (LLMs Do NOT Know What They Don't Know 2025); and truth is linearly decodable (Geometry of Truth 2023). CRITICALLY, none ask whether the RECOGNITION/FAMILIARITY signal CONTAMINATES the TRUTH judgment — whether merely recognizing an entity inflates the internally-decoded belief that a claim about it is true,